course: dictionary
lesson: 3007
title: Everyday words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A dustpan is a flat pan with a handle. You sweep dust and dirt into it with a small brush. Dust and pan are two smaller words joined together, so a dustpan is a pan for dust. Try this trick with other long words: look for smaller words inside them.
explain: Read the clues in the sentence. «Broken glass splits into thin, sharp edges, so it is swept up carefully with a brush and dustpan, never picked up with bare hands.» The word sharp tells you why the glass is swept, not picked up. The dustpan is the tool that keeps your hands safe.
explain: Sentences can also tell you the order of steps. «Glass is picked up with a dustpan and brush and a damp paper towel for tiny pieces, never bare fingers, and wrapped in paper before the bin.» Read the whole list of steps before you decide what to do first.
fact: A dustpan is a flat pan with a handle.
fact: You sweep dust and dirt into a dustpan with a small brush.
fact: Dustpan is made from two words: dust and pan.
fact: «Dustpan and brush» is used to clean up crumbs, dirt and broken glass.
fact: For broken glass, use a dustpan and brush and a damp paper towel for tiny pieces, and never use bare fingers.
exercise: «Broken glass splits into thin, sharp edges, so it is swept up carefully with a brush and dustpan, never picked up with bare hands.» What is a dustpan used for? | Carrying hot water | *Sweeping dust and dirt into it | Drying wet hands | Holding a cup of tea
exercise: Dustpan is made from two smaller words. Which are they? | pan and brush | dust and bin | *dust and pan | sweep and pan
exercise: «Glass is picked up with a dustpan and brush and a damp paper towel for tiny pieces, never bare fingers, and wrapped in paper before the bin.» Why never bare fingers? | Because paper towels are cleaner | *Because the glass is sharp and could cut you | Because fingers are too big for the glass | Because the glass is too hot to touch
test:
What is a dustpan? | A brush with a long handle | *A flat pan with a handle, for sweeping dust and dirt into | A bin with a lid | A cloth for wiping tables
test:
In the sentences, what must you do with broken glass before it goes in the bin? | Throw it straight in | *Wrap it in paper | Leave it on the floor | Pour water on it
exam:
Which is the safest way to clean up broken glass, according to the sentences? | Pick it up with bare fingers | Throw it straight into the bin | *Sweep it with a brush into a dustpan | Leave it on the floor for someone else
